# REGRESSION PIN — a `newtype` over a GENERIC payload, both halves of the fix.
#
# WRONG BEFORE THE FIX (measured at pristine HEAD):
#     C and LLVM → `gg build` rc 1
#     LLVM `llc`: "void type only allowed for function results: load void, ptr"
#     C:          -Wint-conversion, the payload pointer truncated into `_0: Unit`
#
# TWO INDEPENDENT DEFECTS, and this cell reddens on EITHER revert:
#   (1) REGISTRATION — `register_newtype` called the NON-registering
#       `mapper.map_ast_type(...)` (= `try_map_ast_type(ty).unwrap_or(UNIT_TYPE)`),
#       so `Vector[int]` was never registered and `_0` lowered to `Unit`. Its
#       immediate sibling `register_struct` already used `map_ast_type_mut`, with
#       a comment saying exactly why. Revert it → build rc 1 again.
#   (2) STRUCTINIT — the construction stayed an `Expr::Call`, so it never reached
#       `move_zero_consumed_args` and both backends re-derived it by name-match.
#       Revert it → C traps `index out of bounds` on `a.0[1]`, LLVM rc 134
#       `double free detected in tcache 2`.
#
# ⚠ (2) IS WHY (1) CANNOT SHIP ALONE. With only the registration half, this
# program goes from a LOUD BUILD FAILURE to a bounds trap on C and a double free
# on LLVM — up the ratified severity ladder (Core #8). Both halves land together.
#
# ⚠ Reads the payload back (`len()` AND an index) rather than printing "built":
# a construction-only assertion is green on a compiler that stores garbage.
newtype NV(Vector[int])

void main():
    Vector[int] v = [10, 20, 30]
    NV a = NV(v)
    print(a.0.len())
    print(a.0[1])
